# Relay audit context for Cursor

Full audit: `docs/RELAY-AUDIT-vs-METRICOOL-BUFFER.md`.

Relay is a local, MCP-native publisher for X, Threads, TikTok, YouTube and Instagram.
It is strong at publishing, scheduling, validation, Threads comment replies and
agent automation. It is **not** yet a Metricool/Buffer replacement for analytics,
unified inbox, approvals, calendar, media library, link-in-bio, ads or teams.

## What to remember

- Relay MCP tools: `relay_accounts`, `relay_connect`, `relay_disconnect`,
  `relay_post`, `relay_validate`, `relay_queue`, `relay_cancel`,
  `relay_history`, `relay_threads_comments`, `relay_threads_autoreply`,
  `relay_threads_reply`, `relay_limits`, `relay_console`.
- Always call `relay_validate` before `relay_post`.
- Threads replies are explicit-only; never auto-post a reply.
- YouTube is one video per post; quota ≈ 6 uploads/day.
- Instagram needs a public media URL and a Business/Creator account.
- X needs pay-per-use credits; Threads needs the Meta app in good standing.
- Keep one Relay server running so the scheduler can publish queued posts.

## Common commands

```powershell
npm run batch -- content/plans/week.json --dry-run
npm run batch -- content/plans/week.json
npm run youtube-max -- --dir "C:\path\to\videos" --privacy public
```

## Gaps to prioritize

P0: analytics, unified inbox, approvals/roles, calendar + media library.
P1: LinkedIn/Facebook/Pinterest/Bluesky/GBP, link-in-bio, built-in AI, integrations, mobile/PWA.
P2: ads, competitors, hashtags, white-label reports, hosted API/webhooks.
